# a-unit-of-work-that-fails

Alice's closure, with one unit of work somewhere in it that does not commit: it rolls back, 
or it commits and the process dies before the outbox is sent. A rollback leaves the record 
where it was, since the offset never moved, so the question is not whether the work happens 
but whether anything the portal already promised can come apart from it. 

